# AREA in the hyperbolic plane, in differential form: the identities whose integrals are the area theorems. On the
# hyperboloid (space/hyperbolic/hyperboloid) the geodesic through a point u with unit tangent v is
#
#   x(s) = cosh(s) u + sinh(s) v,   written with c = cosh s, s = sinh s, c^2 - s^2 = 1,
#
# and d/ds is the DERIVATION D with D c = s and D s = c (u and v are constant), so D x = d := s u + c v and D d = x.
# Every statement below is an identity in the polynomial ring, proved for all values. Where it has hypotheses (u a
# point, v a unit tangent at u, c and s a cosh and sinh) it is written as a CERTIFICATE, as in space/hyperbolic/metric:
# the difference of its two sides as a sum of multiples of the hypotheses' differences, so it holds whenever they do.
#
#   THE GEODESIC        x stays on the hyperboloid and d is a unit tangent to it (the flow D keeps c^2 - s^2, since
#                       D (c^2 - s^2) = 2 c s - 2 s c);
#   ANGULAR MOMENTUM    N = x1 d2 - x2 d1 is constant along the geodesic: D N = 0, by the product rule and D d = x;
#   THE TURNING         with r the distance from the origin (cosh r = x0, sinh^2 r = x1^2 + x2^2), theta the polar
#                       angle and psi the angle between the geodesic and the radial direction:
#                         (sinh^2 r) D theta = N,   tan psi = N / M with M = D x0 = d0,
#                       so D psi = (M D N - N D M) / (M^2 + N^2) = -N x0 / (M^2 + N^2). The identity proved here is
#                         M^2 + N^2 = x1^2 + x2^2 = sinh^2 r,
#                       which makes D psi = -cosh r D theta: the geodesic turns away from the radial direction at
#                       cosh r times the rate the polar angle turns. This is the GAUSS-BONNET INTEGRAND;
#   THE DISK            the circle of radius r is traced at speed sinh r (space/hyperbolic/metric), so the area
#                       element in polar coordinates is sinh r dr dtheta, and cosh r - 1 is the antiderivative of
#                       sinh r that vanishes at r = 0 (D cosh = sinh, cosh 0 = 1): the disk area's integrand.
#
# What integration then gives, with the fundamental theorem of calculus as the one step not proved here:
#
#   the disk of radius r has area  integral over theta of integral_0^r sinh = 2 pi (cosh r - 1);
#   a triangle with a vertex at the origin, angle alpha there, and far side the geodesic, has area
#     integral_0^alpha (cosh r - 1) d theta = integral (-D psi - D theta) = psi(start) - psi(end) - alpha,
#   which is pi minus its three angles: AREA EQUALS DEFECT (Gauss-Bonnet), and every triangle is a sum of two of these.
#
# The fundamental theorem of calculus itself needs the real numbers (K4 in note/term/port/kernel-prerequisites.md):
# every algebraic step above is proved, and that one analytic step is what remains.

# THE GEODESIC. B(x, x) - 1, for x = c u + s v, is a combination of the hypotheses' differences: it is 0 whenever u is
# a point (B(u, u) = 1), v a unit tangent (B(v, v) = -1, B(u, v) = 0) and c^2 - s^2 = 1.
rule the-geodesic-stays-on-the-hyperboloid
  seat u0, like integer
  seat u1, like integer
  seat u2, like integer
  seat v0, like integer
  seat v1, like integer
  seat v2, like integer
  seat c, like integer
  seat s, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call subtract
        call subtract
          call subtract
            call multiply
              call add
                call multiply
                  read c
                  read u0
                call multiply
                  read s
                  read v0
              call add
                call multiply
                  read c
                  read u0
                call multiply
                  read s
                  read v0
            call multiply
              call add
                call multiply
                  read c
                  read u1
                call multiply
                  read s
                  read v1
              call add
                call multiply
                  read c
                  read u1
                call multiply
                  read s
                  read v1
          call multiply
            call add
              call multiply
                read c
                read u2
              call multiply
                read s
                read v2
            call add
              call multiply
                read c
                read u2
              call multiply
                read s
                read v2
        code 1
      call add
        call add
          call add
            call multiply
              call multiply
                read c
                read c
              call subtract
                call subtract
                  call subtract
                    call multiply
                      read u0
                      read u0
                    call multiply
                      read u1
                      read u1
                  call multiply
                    read u2
                    read u2
                code 1
            call multiply
              call multiply
                call multiply
                  code 2
                  read c
                read s
              call subtract
                call subtract
                  call multiply
                    read u0
                    read v0
                  call multiply
                    read u1
                    read v1
                call multiply
                  read u2
                  read v2
          call multiply
            call multiply
              read s
              read s
            call add
              call subtract
                call subtract
                  call multiply
                    read v0
                    read v0
                  call multiply
                    read v1
                    read v1
                call multiply
                  read v2
                  read v2
              code 1
        call subtract
          call subtract
            call multiply
              read c
              read c
            call multiply
              read s
              read s
          code 1

# Its velocity d = D x = s u + c v has B(d, d) = -1: the geodesic is traced at unit speed.
rule the-geodesic-velocity-is-a-unit-vector
  seat u0, like integer
  seat u1, like integer
  seat u2, like integer
  seat v0, like integer
  seat v1, like integer
  seat v2, like integer
  seat c, like integer
  seat s, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call add
        call subtract
          call subtract
            call multiply
              call add
                call multiply
                  read s
                  read u0
                call multiply
                  read c
                  read v0
              call add
                call multiply
                  read s
                  read u0
                call multiply
                  read c
                  read v0
            call multiply
              call add
                call multiply
                  read s
                  read u1
                call multiply
                  read c
                  read v1
              call add
                call multiply
                  read s
                  read u1
                call multiply
                  read c
                  read v1
          call multiply
            call add
              call multiply
                read s
                read u2
              call multiply
                read c
                read v2
            call add
              call multiply
                read s
                read u2
              call multiply
                read c
                read v2
        code 1
      call subtract
        call add
          call add
            call multiply
              call multiply
                read s
                read s
              call subtract
                call subtract
                  call subtract
                    call multiply
                      read u0
                      read u0
                    call multiply
                      read u1
                      read u1
                  call multiply
                    read u2
                    read u2
                code 1
            call multiply
              call multiply
                call multiply
                  code 2
                  read c
                read s
              call subtract
                call subtract
                  call multiply
                    read u0
                    read v0
                  call multiply
                    read u1
                    read v1
                call multiply
                  read u2
                  read v2
          call multiply
            call multiply
              read c
              read c
            call add
              call subtract
                call subtract
                  call multiply
                    read v0
                    read v0
                  call multiply
                    read v1
                    read v1
                call multiply
                  read v2
                  read v2
              code 1
        call subtract
          call subtract
            call multiply
              read c
              read c
            call multiply
              read s
              read s
          code 1

# And B(x, d) = 0: the velocity is tangent to the hyperboloid at x.
rule the-geodesic-velocity-is-tangent
  seat u0, like integer
  seat u1, like integer
  seat u2, like integer
  seat v0, like integer
  seat v1, like integer
  seat v2, like integer
  seat c, like integer
  seat s, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call subtract
        call subtract
          call multiply
            call add
              call multiply
                read c
                read u0
              call multiply
                read s
                read v0
            call add
              call multiply
                read s
                read u0
              call multiply
                read c
                read v0
          call multiply
            call add
              call multiply
                read c
                read u1
              call multiply
                read s
                read v1
            call add
              call multiply
                read s
                read u1
              call multiply
                read c
                read v1
        call multiply
          call add
            call multiply
              read c
              read u2
            call multiply
              read s
              read v2
          call add
            call multiply
              read s
              read u2
            call multiply
              read c
              read v2
      call add
        call add
          call multiply
            call multiply
              read c
              read s
            call subtract
              call subtract
                call subtract
                  call multiply
                    read u0
                    read u0
                  call multiply
                    read u1
                    read u1
                call multiply
                  read u2
                  read u2
              code 1
          call multiply
            call add
              call multiply
                read c
                read c
              call multiply
                read s
                read s
            call subtract
              call subtract
                call multiply
                  read u0
                  read v0
                call multiply
                  read u1
                  read v1
              call multiply
                read u2
                read v2
        call multiply
          call multiply
            read c
            read s
          call add
            call subtract
              call subtract
                call multiply
                  read v0
                  read v0
                call multiply
                  read v1
                  read v1
              call multiply
                read v2
                read v2
            code 1

# ANGULAR MOMENTUM. D N for N = x1 d2 - x2 d1, by the product rule with D x = d and D d = x, is
# (d1 d2 + x1 x2) - (d2 d1 + x2 x1) = 0.
rule angular-momentum-is-conserved
  seat u0, like integer
  seat u1, like integer
  seat u2, like integer
  seat v0, like integer
  seat v1, like integer
  seat v2, like integer
  seat c, like integer
  seat s, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call subtract
        call add
          call multiply
            call add
              call multiply
                read s
                read u1
              call multiply
                read c
                read v1
            call add
              call multiply
                read s
                read u2
              call multiply
                read c
                read v2
          call multiply
            call add
              call multiply
                read c
                read u1
              call multiply
                read s
                read v1
            call add
              call multiply
                read c
                read u2
              call multiply
                read s
                read v2
        call add
          call multiply
            call add
              call multiply
                read s
                read u2
              call multiply
                read c
                read v2
            call add
              call multiply
                read s
                read u1
              call multiply
                read c
                read v1
          call multiply
            call add
              call multiply
                read c
                read u2
              call multiply
                read s
                read v2
            call add
              call multiply
                read c
                read u1
              call multiply
                read s
                read v1
      code 0

# THE TURNING, for any point x and tangent d (not only on one geodesic): M^2 + N^2 - sinh^2 r, with M = d0 and
# N = x1 d2 - x2 d1, is the certificate below in h1 = B(x, x) - 1, h2 = B(d, d) + 1 and h3 = B(x, d). So where x is a
# point and d a unit tangent at it, M^2 + N^2 = x1^2 + x2^2 = sinh^2 r and D psi = -cosh r D theta.
rule the-gauss-bonnet-turning-identity
  seat x0, like integer
  seat x1, like integer
  seat x2, like integer
  seat d0, like integer
  seat d1, like integer
  seat d2, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call subtract
        call add
          call multiply
            read d0
            read d0
          call multiply
            call subtract
              call multiply
                read x1
                read d2
              call multiply
                read x2
                read d1
            call subtract
              call multiply
                read x1
                read d2
              call multiply
                read x2
                read d1
        call add
          call multiply
            read x1
            read x1
          call multiply
            read x2
            read x2
      call add
        call subtract
          call multiply
            call add
              call subtract
                call subtract
                  call multiply
                    read d0
                    read d0
                  call multiply
                    read d1
                    read d1
                call multiply
                  read d2
                  read d2
              code 1
            call add
              call subtract
                code 1
                call multiply
                  read x0
                  read x0
              call subtract
                call subtract
                  call subtract
                    call multiply
                      read x0
                      read x0
                    call multiply
                      read x1
                      read x1
                  call multiply
                    read x2
                    read x2
                code 1
          call multiply
            call multiply
              call subtract
                call subtract
                  call subtract
                    call multiply
                      read x0
                      read x0
                    call multiply
                      read x1
                      read x1
                  call multiply
                    read x2
                    read x2
                code 1
              read d0
            read d0
        call multiply
          call subtract
            call subtract
              call multiply
                read x0
                read d0
              call multiply
                read x1
                read d1
            call multiply
              read x2
              read d2
          call subtract
            call multiply
              call multiply
                code 2
                read x0
              read d0
            call subtract
              call subtract
                call multiply
                  read x0
                  read d0
                call multiply
                  read x1
                  read d1
              call multiply
                read x2
                read d2
